WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.463
Two ways to place an order.

2
00:00:01.583 --> 00:00:04.346
A market order prioritizes execution.

3
00:00:04.466 --> 00:00:06.707
A limit order sets a price condition.

4
00:00:07.227 --> 00:00:08.678
Market: trade now.

5
00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:11.294
Sprout fills at its displayed simulated quote.

6
00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:14.340
Real market orders may fill at a different price.

7
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.462
Buy limit: at or below.

8
00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:21.725
With a $100 buy limit, the purchase can fill at $100 or less.

9
00:00:21.845 --> 00:00:24.214
It cannot fill above $100.

10
00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:26.221
A limit may never fill.

11
00:00:26.341 --> 00:00:30.265
If the price stays above $100, that buy limit waits.

12
00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:32.974
A chosen price is not a guaranteed trade.

13
00:00:33.494 --> 00:00:34.551
Practice both.

14
00:00:34.671 --> 00:00:37.387
Sprout checks pending limits while the app is open.

15
00:00:37.507 --> 00:00:41.095
Real trading has spreads, slippage, and other costs.

